  <prompt>Wire CreateEventWizard.tsx to actually consume the initialAssociation/lockAssociation seed VisualHostRoot now passes (task 012), bump the VisualHost PCF version, build:prod + pack + deploy per pcf-deploy, and smoke-test creating an Event from a Matter visual.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE PCF + shared-UI developer. Follow pcf-deploy exactly (build:prod, shared-lib installed first) AND the ADR-024 associateToStep pattern from CreateTodoWizard/TodoWizardDialog.tsx.</role>
  <goal>VisualHost deployed with a working "+" → CreateEventWizard flow; a created Event is regarding the host Matter with all resolver fields populated; a document dual-binds to Matter + Event.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      VisualHost imports shared-lib SOURCE — the shared lib node_modules must be installed before build:prod. Bump all 5 version locations.

      **Task 002 (completed)**: the new sprk_document→sprk_event lookup was created with SchemaName "sprk_Event" (verified against live Dataverse metadata to match the existing sprk_Invoice/sprk_WorkAssignment PascalCase convention) — this is the EXACT literal string CreateEventWizard.tsx:254-257 already hardcodes in its `createDocumentRecords('sprk_events', eventId, 'sprk_Event', ...)` call. No code change needed for the document dual-bind itself; verify it during the smoke test rather than assuming.

      **🔴 Scope expansion discovered 2026-07-08 (post-012 review) — CreateEventWizard.tsx has NO Associate-To step at all today.** Traced concretely:
      - `ICreateEventWizardProps` has no `initialAssociation`/`lockAssociation` fields.
      - `CreateEventWizard`'s `config: ICreateRecordWizardConfig` object has no `associateToStep` entry at all (not even present-but-unlocked) — the wizard goes straight Add Files → Event Details → Next Steps with zero association capability.
      - `eventService.ts:249` — `createEvent(formValues, regardingEntityName?, options?)` was already migrated (task 014) to accept an optional `regardingEntityName` + read `formValues.regardingRecordId`/`regardingRecordName`, and internally calls `applyResolverFields` when supplied. But `CreateEventWizard.tsx`'s current `onFinish` calls `eventService.createEvent(currentFormValues)` with ONLY one argument — the resolver path is never actually exercised today.
      - Task 012 (VisualHostRoot) already passes `initialAssociation`/`lockAssociation=true` as props into whatever wizard the registry resolves — but since `CreateEventWizard` doesn't read those props at all yet, they are silently dropped. Without this task's wiring, the Visual Host "+" → Event flow will create an Event but it will NOT be regarding the host record — this task's own smoke test would fail.

      **The exact reference pattern to copy** is `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateTodoWizard/TodoWizardDialog.tsx` (the only existing wizard using `associateToStep` today):
      ```ts
      associateToStep: navigationService
        ? { entityTypes: EVENT_REGARDING_TARGETS.slice(), navigationService, initialAssociation, lockAssociation }
        : undefined,
      // ...
      onFinish: async (context) => {
        const result = await eventService.createEvent(currentFormValues, context.association?.entityType, ...);
        // also copy context.association.recordId/.recordName onto formValues.regardingRecordId/.regardingRecordName
        // before calling createEvent, per eventService.createEvent's JSDoc contract (reads them off formValues).
      }
      ```
      Note `TodoWizardDialog`'s `associateToStep` config shown above does NOT yet pass `lockAssociation` (it predates task 014) — you ARE adding `lockAssociation` to `CreateEventWizard`'s config (task 014 already added `lockAssociation` support to `CreateRecordWizard`/`AssociateToStep` — read `CreateRecordWizard.tsx` around `config.associateToStep` handling to confirm the exact field name and behavior: when `lockAssociation` is true, the step is hidden entirely but the seeded `initialAssociation` still reaches `onFinish` via `context.association`).

      **entityTypes list**: `AssociateToStep/types.ts` has `TODO_REGARDING_TARGETS` (11 entries) but it's sprk_todo-specific and doesn't match Event's actual schema. Build a new `EVENT_REGARDING_TARGETS` (or confirm/reuse an existing one if you find it already added) from Event's REAL live-schema lookups — confirmed via Phase 0 discovery (`describe('tables/sprk_event')`): `sprk_regardingmatter`, `sprk_regardingproject`, `sprk_regardinginvoice`, `sprk_regardingaccount`, `sprk_regardingcontact`, `sprk_regardingworkassignment`, `sprk_regardinganalysis`, `sprk_regardingbudget`, `sprk_regardingorganziation` (NOTE: this field name has a typo in live schema — "organziation" not "organization" — use the EXACT live field name, do not "fix" the typo, that would break the lookup). This list matters mainly for future non-locked launch contexts (nothing currently opens CreateEventWizard unlocked with a picker) — get it right, but don't over-invest; the CRITICAL path for THIS task's acceptance criteria is the locked (`lockAssociation=true`) Visual Host launch, which bypasses the picker UI entirely and just needs `context.association` to carry the seeded `initialAssociation` through to `onFinish`.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      src/client/pcf/VisualHost/ (control + Solution)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateEventWizard/CreateEventWizard.tsx (add associateToStep + wire onFinish)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateEventWizard/eventService.ts (createEvent signature — already migrated, do not re-modify without reason)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateTodoWizard/TodoWizardDialog.tsx (canonical associateToStep reference)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/AssociateToStep/types.ts (RegardingTarget shape; add EVENT_REGARDING_TARGETS here)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/CreateRecordWizard.tsx (lockAssociation handling, context.association)
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
