  <steps>
    <step>Verify wizardRegistry 'event' → migrated CreateEventWizard (already true per task 011).</step>
    <step>Add `initialAssociation?: AssociationResult` + `lockAssociation?: boolean` to `ICreateEventWizardProps`; add `EVENT_REGARDING_TARGETS` to `AssociateToStep/types.ts` from Event's real schema (see background — exact live field names, including the "organziation" typo); add `associateToStep` to CreateEventWizard's `config` object (gated on `navigationService` presence, mirroring TodoWizardDialog); wire `onFinish` to read `context.association` and pass it into `eventService.createEvent(formValues, context.association?.entityType)` after copying `context.association.recordId`/`.recordName` onto `formValues.regardingRecordId`/`.regardingRecordName`.</step>
    <step>Verify (no code change expected beyond the above) that CreateEventWizard.tsx's hardcoded 'sprk_Event' nav-prop string in its document dual-bind call now resolves against the sprk_document→sprk_event lookup task 002 created — confirm during the smoke test below rather than assuming.</step>
    <step>Install shared-lib node_modules; bump VisualHost version (all 5 locations); npm run build:prod. NOTE (per task 012 findings): baseline bundle was 741 KiB before task 012's `@spaarke/auth` wiring, which grew it to ~1.19 MiB (structural cost of `@azure/msal-browser` entering the graph for the first time — expected, not a regression). This task's own delta on top of that should be small (a few KB, from the new associateToStep wiring); report the actual before/after.</step>
    <step>Copy artifacts; pack.ps1. Provide the solution ZIP path for import (or import per pcf-deploy).</step>
    <step>Smoke: on a Matter's Events visual, click "+", verify the Associate-To step is HIDDEN (locked to the Matter), complete CreateEventWizard, submit; inspect the Event's regarding lookup + all 5 resolver fields in Dataverse; upload a file and confirm it appears in both the Matter and Event Documents subgrids.</step>
    <step>Regression: open CreateEventWizard from its existing Code Page entry point (src/solutions/CreateEventWizard/src/main.tsx) if reasonably reachable, or at minimum confirm via code review that omitting initialAssociation/lockAssociation (the Code Page's main.tsx doesn't pass either today) still renders a sane wizard (either the step doesn't render because navigationService is absent there too, or renders unlocked+empty) — no crash, no regression to that existing surface.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>Read, Grep, Edit, Bash, PowerShell, Skill(pcf-deploy), Skill(ui-test)</tools>
  <outputs>Deployed VisualHost solution ZIP; CreateEventWizard associateToStep wiring; smoke-test results.</outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>"+" on an Event visual opens CreateEventWizard with the Associate-To step hidden; created Event regarding the host Matter with all 5 resolver fields.</criterion>
