    <step7-code-page-regression-resolution>
      RESOLVED via Path C (precise gating), not escalated to a human decision — the POML explicitly
      offered this as one of two acceptable resolutions ("gate more precisely... or flag for human
      judgment"). Confirmed by reading src/solutions/CreateEventWizard/src/main.tsx:81-92: it DOES
      pass navigationService={navigationService} to CreateEventWizard, but passes NEITHER
      initialAssociation NOR lockAssociation. A gate mirroring TodoWizardDialog verbatim
      (navigationService-only) would have surfaced a brand-new, unlocked, un-seeded Associate-To
      step on that already-shipped surface — a real UX regression (an extra required
      click/Skip on every standalone Event creation).
      Fix: resolveEventAssociateToStepConfig() in CreateEventWizard.tsx requires navigationService
      AND (initialAssociation !== undefined OR lockAssociation === true). This exactly preserves
      the Code Page's current behavior (associateToStep resolves to undefined — zero change) while
      enabling the Visual Host locked-launch path (initialAssociation set + lockAssociation=true).
      Unit-tested explicitly: "returns undefined when navigationService is present but neither
      initialAssociation nor lockAssociation is set (Code Page regression guard)".
    </step7-code-page-regression-resolution>

